## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-world concerns: consent governance, dynamic schema evolution, cross-region data lineage, residency, and auditable privacy controls.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant consent governance and field-level filtering
- Edge filtering and region-local routing
- Schema evolution via Avro + schema registry with versioning
- Tamper-evident, immutable audit logs for lineage
- DSAR testing, data portability, and deletion guarantees

## Code Example
```javascript
function filterFieldsByConsent(event, consentMap) {
  const allowed = consentMap[event.tenant_id] || [];
  const filtered = {};
  for (const k of Object.keys(event)) {
    if (allowed.includes(k)) filtered[k] = event[k];
  }
  return filtered;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to handle consent updates mid-stream without data loss?
- What metrics validate data minimization and retention policy?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design a sophisticated, multi-tenant feature store that addresses critical fintech requirements including data residency, privacy protection, and operational reliability.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-tenant data isolation and residency compliance
- Local differential privacy for feature-level protection
- Immutable versioned storage with automated lifecycle management
- Statistical drift detection and comprehensive access governance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code for privacy-aware ingestion
function ingestFeature(event) {
  // Apply tenant-specific privacy masking
  const maskedEvent = applyLocalDP(event, event.tenant_id);

  // Route to regional cluster based on residency requirements
  const region = getRegionByTenant(event.tenant_id);

  // Version and store with immutable timestamp
  return storeFeature(maskedEvent, region);
}
```
